Upstream core/message/content/property/context/conversion/tool-argument-streaming
regression tests are adapted under test/upstream-*.test.ts. Additional tests cover
standalone lifecycle/auth/embedding/discovery and actual local HTTP protocols.

Standalone integration replaces Cordis, session/settings/home services and timer
plugins with explicit provider/credential/attachment ports. It has no dependency
on the AI Employee OS platform. Runtime, retry policy execution and independent
OpenAI embeddings are adapted for ordinary Node.js projects.

Bundled dependency: @earendil-works/pi-ai exactly 1.3.0 (MIT).
Its full published package, original licenses and transitive runtime dependencies
are included via npm bundleDependencies. Six distributed dist/api JavaScript files
carry the above Harness patch. dist/pi-ai-patch-manifest.json records their SHA256
identities, and scripts/verify-consumer.mjs verifies the installed tarball contents.
No consumer postinstall script or pnpm patch mechanism is required.

This SDK provides protocol implementations and catalog metadata, not a claim that
every catalog provider/model/account was tested against its live service. Tests
use local HTTP fixtures only; real model requests and OAuth logins were not run.
